  "notes": "DOUBT: chfs.ky.gov returns HTTP 403 to this network (and to WebFetch), so the official PDF was obtained from an unaltered Wayback Machine capture (id_ raw mode, 2026-07-26) of the official chfs.ky.gov URL. A NEWER official edition exists that could not be downloaded: 'KY Medicaid Dental Fee Schedule 2026 Revised 8.17.2026' (https://www.chfs.ky.gov/agencies/dms/DMSFeeRateSchedules/2026DentalFeeSchedule81926.pdf), which per search-engine snippets states 'dental rebasing is effective 7/1/2026' and shows D0120 at $34.00 (vs $27.50 here). The fees recorded here are therefore the PRE-rebasing rates in force until 2026-06-30 and are likely outdated for many codes. Columns: 'UNDER AGE 21 Rate' -> child, 'OVER AGE 21 RATE' -> adult; 'n/c' = not covered (not_covered_child/adult). Values from the 'Dentist Procedures and Fee Schedule' section; where the 'Oral Surgeon Procedures and Fee Schedule' section lists a different rate it is recorded as child_oral_surgeon/adult_oral_surgeon (D0330 adult, D7220-D7241, D9222/D9223). Orthodontics are paid per case by severity (not D8070-D8090 fee lines): early phase $1367 orthodontist/$1234 general dentist; moderately severe $1825/$1659; severe $3000/$2674; paid 2/3 then 1/3 after six monthly visits; D8670 n/c.",
